2026-02-01 23:33:30,398 - DocumentGraderNode - INFO: Retrieved document Is NPV or ROI More Important?

Both NPV and ROI (return on investment) are important, but they serve different purposes. NPV provides a dollar amount that indicates the projected profitability of an investment, considering the time value of money. Conversely, ROI expresses an investment's efficiency as a percentage, showing the return relative to the investment cost. NPV is often preferred for [capital budgeting](https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/capitalbudgeting.asp) because it gives a direct measure of added value, while ROI is useful for comparing the efficiency of multiple investments. is relevant
