Return on assets (ROA) and ROE are similar in that they both try to gauge how efficiently the company generates its profits. However, ROE compares net income to net assets (assets minus liabilities) of the company, while ROA compares net income to the company’s assets *without* deducting its liabilities. In both cases, companies in industries in which operations require significant assets will likely show a lower average return. is relevant
